  "full_text": "So, like, Diana's getting, like, snail mail from people and stuff. And Terry would be like, does Terry hurt? No, it doesn't hurt. The snail mail from other people doesn't hurt. Then she started, like, being humble. Now it starts to hurt. So, like, Terry would be thinking, am I a brave heart? Am I going to put myself in a position to get zapped again? And, you know, you can work out the logic and the reverse logic and double scheme and scheme. You know, okay, so if I got to go local, then that means I got to go to the church and then get a local person. And then, like, Diana can get the snail mail and get, that's the one she's supposed to go for. And, like, no, no, you're supposed to, like, you know, like, like, he knows that I know. But does he know that I know that he knows that I know? No, no, he knows that I know that he does. Okay, so, like, so, like, Terry be saying, you know. It's basically a dumb scheme. When I scratch my head, do I want to fucking go for Nana and get fucking zapped? I'm saying, no, I don't want to do this. Does it hurt when she fucking gets a snail mail from another person? No, it doesn't hurt. Does it hurt when she starts getting humble? Ow. Okay, hold on. Fuck this. Fuck this. Am I a brave heart? No. Fuck no. Fuck that shit. I'm going to church. Fuck it. You just got to go with your heart. I do not want to get fucking zapped again in a fucking heart. Fuck that shit. You can go fucking do your fucking... This is not for me, man. I'm not into that fucking shit. I ain't gonna fucking fuck around all day getting no emails. Fuck that shit. Get the fuck out, bitch. I go local, man. Fuck all that.",
